tic."],"label":"Ampicillin","obo_id":"mesh:D000667","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_201445","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["disodium;(2S,5R,6R)-6-[[(2R)-2-amino-2-phenylacetyl]amino]-3,3-dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1-azabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-2-carboxylate;(1R,4S)-3,3-dimethyl-2,2,6-trioxo-2lambda6-thiabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-4-carboxylate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_201445","description":[],"label":"Ampicillin Sodium Mixture With Sulbactam Sodium","obo_id":"CHEBI:201445","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["disodium;(2S,5R,6R)-6-[[(2R)-2-amino-2-phenylacetyl]amino]-3,3-dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1-azabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-2-carboxylate;(1R,4S)-3,3-dimethyl-2,2,6-trioxo-2lambda6-thiabicyclo[3.2.0]heptane-4-carboxylate"]},{"iri":"http://snomed.info/id/1148476006","ontology_name":"snomed","ontology_prefix":"SNOMED","short_form":"SNOMED_1148476006","description":[],"label":"Product containing precisely ampicillin 250 milligram and flucloxacillin (as flucloxacillin sodium) 250 milligram/1 each conventional release oral capsule (clinical drug)","obo_id":"","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C016828","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Ampiclox","Viccillin S (combination), ampicillin sodium salt","Viccillin S (combination), cloxacillin sodium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C016828","description":[],"label":"Viccillin S (combination)","obo_id":"mesh:C016828","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DRON_00066032","ontology_name":"dron","ontology_prefix":"DRON","short_form":"DRON_00066032","description":[],"label":"ampicillin 500 MG / diclofenac sodium 25 MG Delayed Release Oral Tablet","obo_id":"DRON:00066032","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DRON_00066033","ontology_name":"dron","ontology_prefix":"DRON","short_form":"DRON_00066033","description":[],"label":"ampicillin 500 MG / diclofenac sodium 25 MG Oral Tablet","obo_id":"DRON:00066033","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008802","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Bay f 1353","Bay-f 1353","Bayf 1353","Baypen","Melocin","Meslocillin","Mezlin","Mezlocillin Sodium","Mezlocilline","Sodium, Mezlocillin"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D008802","description":["Semisynthetic ampicillin-derived acylureido penicillin. It has been proposed for infections with certain anaerobes and may be useful in inner ear, bile, and CNS infections."],"label":"Mezlocillin","obo_id":"mesh:D008802","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D001390","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Azlin","Azlocillin Sodium","Azlocillin, Sodium","Bay e 6905","Bay-e 6905","Baye 6905","Securopen","Sodium Azlocillin","Sodium, Azlocillin"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D001390","description":["A semisynthetic ampicillin-derived acylureido penicillin."],"label":"Azlocillin","obo_id":"mesh:D001390","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/C086821","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["ampicillinoic acid, (2S-(2alpha(S*(S*)),4alpha))-isomer","ampicillinoic acid, disodium salt, (2R-(2alpha(R*(R*)),4alpha))-isomer","sodium ampicilloate"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_C086821","description":[],"label":"ampicillinoic acid","obo_id":"mesh:C086821","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C28823","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C28823","description":["A combination formulation of the sodium salts of the antibiotic ampicillin and the beta-lactamase inhibitor sulbactam with antibacterial activity. Ampicillin, a broad-spectrum, semisynthetic penicillin, binds to and inactivates penicillin-binding proteins (PBP) located on the inner membrane of the bacterial cell wall, thereby interfering with the cross-linking of peptidoglycan chains necessary for bacterial cell wall strength and rigidity. As a result, the cell wall is weakened and the cell lyses. The sulbactam component irreversibly binds to bacterial beta-lactamase at or near its active site, thereby interfering with substrate binding and inhibiting bacterial metabolism of penicillin and cephalosporin beta-lactam antibiotics, effectively extending their antibiotic spectrum to include many beta-lactam-resistant bacteria."],"label":"Sultamicillin","obo_id":"NCIT:C28823","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["SULTAMICILLIN","Sultamicillin","Unasyn"]},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010878","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["AB Piperacillin","AB-Piperacillin","Cl 227193","Cl-227193","Cl227193","Curasan, Piperacillin","Monosodium Salt, Piperacillin","Pipcil","Pipera Hameln","Pipera-Hameln","Piperacillin Curasan","Piperacillin Fresenius","Piperacillin Hexal","Piperacillin Monosodium Salt","Piperacillin Ratiopharm","Piperacillin Sodium","Piperacillin-Ratiopharm","Pipercillin","Pipracil","Pipril","Salt, Piperacillin Monosodium","Sodium, Piperacillin","T 1220","T-1220","T1220"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D010878","description":["Semisynthetic, broad-spectrum, AMPICILLIN derived ureidopenicillin antibiotic proposed for PSEUDOMONAS infections. It is also used in combination with other antibiotics."],"label":"Piperacillin","obo_id":"mesh:D010878","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C749","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C749","description":["The sodium salt of piperacillin, a broad-spectrum semisynthetic, ampicillin-derived ureidopenicillin antibiotic with bactericidal activity. Piperacillin binds to and inactivates penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs), enzymes located on the inner membrane of the bacterial cell wall, resulting in the weakening of the bacterial cell wall and cell lysis. PBPs participate in the terminal stages of assembling the bacterial cell wall, and in reshaping the cell wall during cell division. Inactivation of PBPs interferes with the cross-linkage of peptidoglycan chains necessary for bacterial cell wall strength and rigidity."],"label":"Piperacillin Sodium","obo_id":"NCIT:C749","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["CL 227, 193","PIPERACILLIN SODIUM","Piperacillin Sodium","Pipracil","Sodium (2S,5R,6R)-6-((R)-2-(4-ethyl-2,3-dioxo-1-piperazinecarboxamido)-2-phenylacetamido)-3,3-dimethyl-7-oxo-4-thia-1-azabicyclo(3.2.0)heptane-2-carboxylate","T-1220"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C87369","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C87369","description":["The monohydrate and sodium salt form of mezlocillin, a broad-spectrum, semisynthetic ampicillin-derived acylureidopenicillin with antibacterial activity. Mezlocillin binds to and inactivates penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs) located on the inner membrane of the bacterial cell wall. Inactivation of PBPs interferes with the cross-linkage of peptidoglycan chains necessary for bacterial cell wall strength and rigidity. This interrupts bacterial cell wall synthesis and results in the weakening of the bacterial cell wall, eventually causing cell lysis."],"label":"Mezlocillin Sodium Monohydrate","obo_id":"NCIT:C87369","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["MEZLOCILLIN SODIUM MONOHYDRATE","Mezlocillin Sodium Monohydrate"]}],"numFound":33,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["","15","mesh","7","NCIT","5","CHEBI","2","DRON","2","XCO","2"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","31","false","2"],"ontologyId":["snomed","13","mesh","7","ncit","5","chebi","2","slm","2","dron","2","xco","2"],"ontologyIri":["","15","https://w3id.org/biopragmatics/resources/mesh/mesh.ofn","7","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","5","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/dron.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/xco.owl","2"],"isObsolete":["false","33","true","1"],"type":["class","33"]}}}